Summary: fails to import R 2.3.1 on windows

Initial Comment:
I tracked it down to a regular expression in
rpy_tools.py that does not match the output of version
2.3.1 of R.

version = re.search("R +([0-9]\.[0-9]\.[0-9])", output)

This expects something like 'R 1.2.3' but R 2.3.1 gives
'R version 2.3.1 ...' when queried by running 'R
--version'.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

