Date: 2006-07-17 13:53

Message:
Logged In: YES 
user_id=545257

Exactly, just had the same problem on Mac OS X (it's not the
only software package that relied on the version output
format of previous R releases).

Suggest changing regexp to 

version =
re.search("R\s+(?:version\s*)?([0-9]\.[0-9]\.[0-9])", output)



